      {
        "id": "p7-q43-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the length of $OC$, in terms of $x$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p7-q43-a-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "OC=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt3}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p7-q43-a-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "CM=\\frac{x}{2}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\angle OCM=30^\\circ",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " in triangle ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "OCM",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "In an equilateral triangle, the centre lies on the angle bisectors and medians. Thus $CM=\\dfrac{x}{2}$ and $\\angle OCM=30^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos30^\\circ&=\\frac{CM}{OC}\\\\OC&=\\frac{x}{2\\cos30^\\circ}\\\\OC&=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt3}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q43-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the proportion of $OM$ with respect to the perpendicular height $AM$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p7-q43-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "OM=\\frac13AM",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p7-q43-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Find ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "OM",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " using ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\tan30^\\circ",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", then compare it with ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "AM=x\\sin60^\\circ",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}OM&=\\frac{x}{2}\\tan30^\\circ\\\\OM&=\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt3}\\\\AM&=x\\sin60^\\circ\\\\AM&=\\frac{\\sqrt3x}{2}\\\\\\frac{OM}{AM}&=\\frac{x/(2\\sqrt3)}{\\sqrt3x/2}\\\\\\frac{OM}{AM}&=\\frac13\\end{align*}$$\nHence, $OM=\\dfrac13AM$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      }
    ]
